 # Contact import preview
 
-Existing action emails is exposed through api.dispatch and python cli.py, accepting one JSON object on stdin and writing one JSON result.
+Actions are routed through `api.dispatch(payload)` and the python `cli.py`
+entry point, which accepts one JSON object on stdin and writes one JSON result
+on stdout.
+
+## Actions
+
+### emails
+
+Returns the list of existing contact email strings, unchanged.
+
+    {"action": "emails", "existing": [{"email": "a@b.com", "name": "A"}]}
+
+### import_contacts
+
+Payload keys: `action`, `csv` (a string of valid CSV syntax, up to 200 rows and
+10000 code points), `existing` (a list of `{email, name}` contact objects whose
+email strings are already unique, normalized, lowercase ASCII).
+
+The CSV is comma-separated with the standard double-quote quoting convention.
+The first record must be exactly the header `email,name` in that order; every
+following record must have exactly two columns. Each email is stripped of
+surrounding whitespace and lowercased, then must contain exactly one `@`,
+nonempty text on both sides and no whitespace anywhere; the stripped name must
+be nonempty. New email addresses are deduplicated after normalization: the first
+CSV occurrence is retained, later repeats are dropped, and anything already
+present in `existing` is dropped. Every record is validated, including
+duplicates that end up skipped.
+
+Returns `{"added": [{"email": ..., "name": ...}, ...], "skipped": <int>}`, where
+`skipped` counts every valid CSV data record that was not added, including
+repeat occurrences. `existing` and the payload are never mutated, even on
+failure. A header-only CSV is valid and yields `{"added": [], "skipped": 0}`;
+an empty CSV string is invalid. Quoted names may contain embedded newlines and
+commas.
+
+Concrete invocation (JSON on stdin, JSON on stdout):
+
+    python cli.py <<'EOF'
+    {"action": "import_contacts", "csv": "email,name\nA@B.COM ,\"Ann, X\"\na@b.com,again\n", "existing": [{"email": "z@y.com", "name": "Z"}]}
+    EOF
+
+prints, with exit status 0:
+
+    {"added": [{"email": "a@b.com", "name": "Ann, X"}], "skipped": 1}
+
+Note that a field is only quoted when the double quote is the very first
+character of that field; otherwise the quote and any leading space are literal
+characters of the field.
+
+## Errors
+
+An invalid header, a record whose column count is not two, an invalid email, an
+empty name, an empty CSV string, or an unknown action raises `ValueError`. The
+CLI reports the message on stderr, exits with status 2, prints nothing on stdout
+and shows no traceback. Successful runs exit 0 with a single JSON document on
+stdout.
